<header class="ref-head"><span class="hero-ornament"></span><h1 class="research-title">24 June in history</h1><p class="ref-lede">5 events that happened on 24 June, from 1314 to 1948.</p></header>
<ol class="day-events"><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb tih-event-hero"><p class="tih-hero-kicker">&#10022; Anniversary of the day</p><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/scotland" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/scotland.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1314 CE <span class="tih-ago">712 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Robert the Bruce routs Edward II at Bannockburn</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">On the second day, Scottish spearmen drove the English army into the burns and marshes near Stirling. Edward II fled, and Scotland's independence was secured until England recognised it in 1328.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/scotland">Scotland</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/england">England</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1497 CE <span class="tih-ago">529 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">John Cabot makes landfall in North America</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Sailing for Henry VII, the Venetian navigator John Cabot landed on the coast, probably of Newfoundland or Cape Breton. His voyage became the basis of later English claims in North America.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/north-america">North America</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/newfoundland">Newfoundland</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1717 CE <span class="tih-ago">309 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Premier Grand Lodge of England is founded</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Four London lodges met at the Goose and Gridiron alehouse to form a Grand Lodge. It marks the beginning of organised modern Freemasonry.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/england">England</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/london">London</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1812 CE <span class="tih-ago">214 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Napoleon's Grande Armée crosses the Niemen into Russia</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Some 450,000 troops in the first wave crossed into Russian territory. By December only a fraction had survived the retreat from Moscow.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag tih-tag-profile" href="/empire/russian-empire">Russian Empire</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/grande-armee">Grande Armée</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/napoleon">Napoleon</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/moscow">Moscow</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1948 CE <span class="tih-ago">78 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Soviet Union begins the Berlin Blockade</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Soviet forces cut road, rail and canal links to West Berlin. The Western Allies responded with an airlift that supplied the city's two million people for eleven months.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/soviet-union">Soviet Union</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/allies">Allies</a></div></div></li></ol>
